        <body>
            <div xml:id="d184">

                <pb facs="0264" n="230" sameAs="frus:frus1870/pg230"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">No. 184.</note>
                <head>Mr. Fish to Baron
                        Gerolt.</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State,</hi><hi
                                rendition="#italic"> Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1870-10-19"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >October</hi> 19, 1870.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>The undersigned, Secretary of State of the United States, has the honor to
                    acknowledge the receipt of the communication of the 12th instant, addressed to
                    him by the envoy extraordinary and minister plenipotentiary <pb facs="0265"
                        n="231" xml:id="pg231"/> of the North German Union, relating to violations
                    of international law alleged to have been perpetrated by French troops.</p>
                <p>The undersigned avails himself of the occasion to renew to Baron Gerolt the
                    assurance of his highest consideration.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>HAMILTON FISH.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
